  "body": "Looking for a home that actually works with your lifestyle and your budget? Tucked away in a prime pocket, 338C Glenvar Road delivers effortless low-maintenance living, elevated sea views, and a clever split-level layout built for modern life.\r\n\r\nWhether you are a first-home buyer wanting flatmates downstairs to help smash the mortgage, or a growing family with teenagers craving their own space, this floor plan nails the brief:\r\n\r\nDownstairs Independence & Outdoor Flow: Two generous bedrooms sit on the lower level, both opening directly out to a private, fully fenced lawn area. Serviced by a full family bathroom, it is an ideal setup for boarders, flatmates, guests, or teens who want their own domain.\r\n\r\nUpstairs Sanctuary: Retreat to your private top-floor master suite complete with a walk-in wardrobe, sleek ensuite, and covered deck for your morning coffee\r\n\r\nEntertainer’s Heart (with Zero Bathroom Queues): The light-filled open-plan living and dining zone anchors the home, featuring a contemporary kitchen, seamless flow to a sun-drenched entertaining area, and a separate guest toilet so visitors never have to use the main bathrooms and nobody is waiting in line during the morning rush.\r\n\r\nLock-Up-and-Leave Living: Complete with a single garage, an additional off-street car park, and ample storage on an easy-care 163m² footprint, your weekends belong to the beach not the lawnmower.\r\n\r\nLeave the car at home and stroll down to Long Bay Village for morning coffee, dinner at the local eateries, or a sunset walk along Long Bay Regional Park and Beach. Near Long Bay Primary, Northcross Intermediate, and Long Bay College, this address locks in long-term value on the North Shore.\r\n\r\nSmart layout, coastal views, two-car parking, and zero wasted maintenance come see how easily you can make this yours. View at our open homes this weekend or get in touch to book a private walkthrough.",
